{"status":"unsupported","reason":"A faithful executable contract cannot be represented by the stated typed AST frontend or Python generated-test bridge. D1 requires arbitrary recursive JSON values and recursive schemas with six distinct node types. D2 requires optional schema fields and dynamic property maps. Active guarantees require recursive validation, sorted dynamic object keys, JSON Pointer escaping, deep-copy and non-mutation behavior, and preservation of arbitrary JSON values. The frontend excludes arbitrary JSON, recursive records, sorting, and the required string escaping operations. Fixed records or bounded examples would narrow the frozen specification, and opaque Lean cannot satisfy the required TESTED assurance.","blocked_obligations":{"O2":["Q1"],"E3":["Q2"]},"open_questions":{"Q1":"Whether required names absent from properties are checked, and their diagnostic traversal positions.","Q2":"Whether enum equality distinguishes booleans from numeric values."},"required_extension":"An executable recursive JSON and schema model with optional fields, dynamic maps, sorted-key traversal, recursive validation, JSON Pointer escaping, and a bridge capable of checking Python purity, deep-copy behavior, and resource constraints."}